      "title": "Orpheus",
      "category":"rock-operas",
      "image": "./src/assets/posters/Orpheus.png",
      "alt": "Orpheus",
      "description": "Olga Vayner’s rock opera 'Orpheus' is a mythological thriller about choice, destiny, and love.The threads of gods’ and mortals’ fates intertwine in an intricate pattern. To bring back his lost beloved, Eurydice, the renowned hero Orpheus descends into the realm of the dead. There, he discovers that during his journey, the earth has been plunged into an endless winter—the result of the goddess Demeter’s grief over her daughter Persephone, who was abducted by Hades. Unwittingly, the hero finds himself at the epicenter of divine intrigues; now, not only his beloved’s future but the fate of the entire mortal world hinges on his decisions.Join us as we descend into the realm of Hades and emerge back into the light alongside Orpheus, finding our own path!",
